## Method

Suite run (PROTOCOL.md): requests are one user message with a fresh nonce first, temperature 0, top_p 1, seed 0, ignore_eos (else logit_bias -100 on the EOS ids) with max_tokens = gen_tokens; t0 is when the last request byte is sent; tokens are counted by re-tokenizing the output with the pinned tokenizer (server counts are kept beside them and may differ by at most 2%); one discarded full-length request per size precedes the first round, and one discarded max_tokens-1 warmup precedes each round; rounds interleave the sizes in a cyclic (Latin-square) order; a cell's statistic is the median of its valid reps, its spread the range normalised to n = 3 with d2; a cell over its gate gets 2 extra reps once, then may drop the one rep farthest from the median, else it is rejected. Concurrency is a closed loop of N clients measured in a window that opens when every client has completed one request.

